        "width": 568,
        "node_type": "markdown_note",
        "name": "note_1",
        "markdown": "The **LLM Code** block is where Rust code is generated from your instruction/prompt.\n\n##### How it works in this recipe:\n\n- You provide a clear prompt (often using Jinja references from earlier columns)\n- The model returns a response\n- The block extracts code content directly for the output column\n\n##### Current status:\n\n- Generated Rust is checked by the **Advanced custom check** block with a Python function that runs `cargo check`\n- Rows that fail the check are filtered out of the final dataset\n\n##### Tip:\n\n- Ask for one self-contained `main.rs` with `fn main()`\n- Ask for explicit error handling\n- Ask for no markdown fences if you want cleaner extraction\n",
        "note_color": "#FEF3C7",
        "note_opacity": "35"
      },
{
        "id": "note_2",
        "x": 2597.376821192053,
        "y": 1233.2039735099338,
        "width": 471,
        "node_type": "markdown_note",
        "name": "note_2",
        "markdown": "The **Advanced custom check** block runs a Python function you write over each generated code cell.\n\n##### How this recipe is set up:\n\n- The Python function writes a `Cargo.toml` and `src/main.rs` into a temp folder and runs `cargo check` with `subprocess`\n- Rows whose code fails `cargo check` are dropped from the final dataset\n- The `rust_check` column itself is kept out of the final output (drop is on)\n\n##### How it differs from the Custom check block:\n\n- The **Custom check** block (as in the Text to Go recipe) runs a tool command template over the generated file\n- The **Advanced custom check** block instead runs arbitrary Python, so the check controls everything: temp files, subprocesses, and the result DataFrame\n- `pd`, `subprocess`, `tempfile` and `Path` are pre-imported; add imports only for modules specific to your code\n\n##### Note:\n\n- The function runs locally, so `cargo` must be installed on this machine\n- New checks require a one-time consent toggle before a run\n",
        "note_color": "#FEF3C7",
        "note_opacity": "35"
      },
